(horn honks twice)

52
00:02:47.014 --> 00:02:48.918
(indistinct chatter)

53
00:02:48.951 --> 00:02:50.722
Hope you haven't
had breakfast yet.

54
00:02:50.755 --> 00:02:52.659
Yeah?

55
00:02:52.692 --> 00:02:54.295
Just did.

56
00:02:54.328 --> 00:02:56.499
Poor guy over there.
fishing with his son

57
00:02:56.534 --> 00:02:57.969
when he spotted the body.

58
00:02:58.003 --> 00:03:00.240
Fishing in the Hudson?
You're shitting me.

59
00:03:00.274 --> 00:03:02.311
(indistinct radio transmission)

60
00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:07.689
Oh. my God. Jesus.

61
00:03:07.722 --> 00:03:10.327
- ID?
- Just this.

62
00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:11.864
The Brownstone.

63
00:03:11.897 --> 00:03:13.977
- It's a fruit stand over on...
- Yeah. I know what it is.

64
00:03:14.001 --> 00:03:17.709
Anything else? I don't
see any visible wounds.

65
00:03:17.743 --> 00:03:19.747
Besides the obvious one.

66
00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:21.325
WOMAN: Neck was severed around
the fourth cervical vertebra.

67
00:03:21.349 --> 00:03:23.320
right through the vocal cords.

68
00:03:23.353 --> 00:03:26.761
Well. at least we know what he
was doing right before he died.

69
00:03:26.794 --> 00:03:28.831
Yeah. Mulcahy?
What was he doing?

70
00:03:28.865 --> 00:03:30.300
Giving head.

71
00:03:30.334 --> 00:03:32.839
(laughter)

72
00:03:32.873 --> 00:03:34.543
HANNAH: The levels
of multiplication

73
00:03:34.576 --> 00:03:36.312
and mutation are more
rapid than anything

74
00:03:36.346 --> 00:03:38.450
- I've ever seen.
- Mm.

75
00:03:38.483 --> 00:03:40.454
And you're sure the samples
were properly handled?

76
00:03:40.487 --> 00:03:41.791
I went out to Fire Island

77
00:03:41.824 --> 00:03:43.493
and collected and
prepared them myself.

78
00:03:43.528 --> 00:03:46.299
WILLIAM: And the symptoms
when they're displayed?

79
00:03:46.332 --> 00:03:48.571
Seizures. skin infection.

80
00:03:48.604 --> 00:03:50.474
liver failure.

81
00:03:51.911 --> 00:03:53.413
You have to get out there.

82
00:03:53.447 --> 00:03:55.517
talk to the mayor.
chief of police.

83
00:03:55.552 --> 00:03:59.025
At this level of mutation
and multiplication.

84
00:03:59.058 --> 00:04:01.964
we can have an epidemic
on our hands in months.

85
00:04:01.997 --> 00:04:03.835
MANNEY: What happened to it?

86
00:04:03.868 --> 00:04:07.341
HANNAH: It has a
virus. a new one.

87
00:04:07.374 --> 00:04:08.921
I've been taking samples
from deer carcasses

88
00:04:08.945 --> 00:04:10.882
out on the island
for over a year.

89
00:04:10.915 --> 00:04:12.995
ever since the first buck
died with similar symptoms.

90
00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:15.658
MANNEY: We've definitely been
finding more dead ones as of late.

91
00:04:15.692 --> 00:04:18.363
One of my deputies found three
dead together the other day.

92
00:04:18.396 --> 00:04:19.933
Looked like a family.

93
00:04:19.967 --> 00:04:22.371
Whatever this virus is.
it's highly communicable.

94
00:04:22.404 --> 00:04:24.375
and it could be
mutating too quickly

95
00:04:24.408 --> 00:04:26.580
for the deer's immune
system to fight it.

96
00:04:26.614 --> 00:04:29.051
LEMBEK: If these deer here
are isolated on an island.

97
00:04:29.085 --> 00:04:32.592
then how the hell did they
suddenly catch some new disease?

98
00:04:32.626 --> 00:04:35.364
New diseases are born
every day. That's science.

99
00:04:35.397 --> 00:04:37.434
As scary as it may seem.

100
00:04:37.468 --> 00:04:39.108
if we don't start
mitigation efforts soon.

101
00:04:39.138 --> 00:04:41.744
it's going to wipe out
the entire population.

102
00:04:41.777 --> 00:04:44.348
You're going to have to kill
all the deer on this island.

103
00:04:44.382 --> 00:04:46.654
LEMBEK: And if we don't.
they're all gonna die?

104
00:04:46.687 --> 00:04:49.626
HANNAH: The deer are simply the
first carriers of the virus.

105
00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:52.398
And the way that it's mutating.
it could leap to humans

106
00:04:52.431 --> 00:04:53.868
if it hasn't already.

107
00:04:54.903 --> 00:04:56.506
Then we're gonna have to arm up

108
00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:58.711
and shoot down every
deer on this island.

109
00:05:01.149 --> 00:05:02.652
(rhythmic. mechanical beeping)

110
00:05:02.686 --> 00:05:04.723
(siren blaring)

111
00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:12.074
Support us and become VIP member 
to remove all ads from www.OpenSubtitles.org

112
00:05:19.686 --> 00:05:22.124
- What do you think?
- WOMAN: Hard to tell.

113
00:05:22.157 --> 00:05:24.495
Rats got to the head.
and the body was deformed

114
00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:26.132
- by the water.
- Right.

115
00:05:26.165 --> 00:05:28.571
Those cuts look
pretty similar to me.

116
00:05:28.604 --> 00:05:30.851
Could be. but I couldn't tell
you if they were the same blade.

117
00:05:30.875 --> 00:05:32.712
Well. come on. It's got to be.

118
00:05:32.746 --> 00:05:34.458
You know. if this was the head
and body of a pretty blonde

119
00:05:34.482 --> 00:05:36.720
16-year-old from Riverdale.
you'd have ten detectives

120
00:05:36.754 --> 00:05:39.125
- down here on the case.
- Hold up.

121
00:05:39.158 --> 00:05:42.699
Someone stuffed it down
in there pretty good.

122
00:05:42.732 --> 00:05:44.435
Holy shit.

123
00:05:44.468 --> 00:05:46.105
Was that the cause of death?

124
00:05:46.139 --> 00:05:47.952
Or could somebody have stuffed
that down there post-mortem?

125
00:05:47.976 --> 00:05:49.746
Teeth are intact. which means

126
00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:52.051
he probably didn't struggle
when it was being put in.

127
00:05:52.084 --> 00:05:55.959
Don't the homosexuals use
colored handkerchiefs like this

128
00:05:55.992 --> 00:05:57.862
to let others know
what they're into?

129
00:05:57.896 --> 00:06:00.969
Saw something about
it on Donahue.

130
00:06:01.937 --> 00:06:03.808
Thanks.

131
00:06:04.810 --> 00:06:06.580
(indistinct chatter)

132
00:06:06.614 --> 00:06:09.051
Where's Gino Barelli?

133
00:06:10.722 --> 00:06:13.426
We want to lodge a
formal complaint.

134
00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:15.430
What do I look like.
your hairdresser?

135
00:06:15.464 --> 00:06:17.602
Ha! Your paper is here to
serve the gay community.

136
00:06:17.636 --> 00:06:19.138
but you're ignoring half of it.

137
00:06:19.171 --> 00:06:21.442
Listen. if you want
to apply for a job

138
00:06:21.476 --> 00:06:23.648
or submit a freelance article

139
00:06:23.681 --> 00:06:26.019
or an op-ed.
please. be my guest.

140
00:06:26.052 --> 00:06:27.822
Hey. lesbians have issues. too.

141
00:06:27.856 --> 00:06:29.902
Why don't you ever write
about women's health issues?

142
00:06:29.926 --> 00:06:32.097
How the ERA is
completely stalled out?

143
00:06:32.131 --> 00:06:34.035
How we can't get access
to health care...

144
00:06:34.068 --> 00:06:35.905
Yeah. Write about that.

145
00:06:35.939 --> 00:06:38.152
You know. I would really love
to write about those issues.

146
00:06:38.176 --> 00:06:41.115
but I'm a gay man. so
I write about issues

147
00:06:41.149 --> 00:06:42.953
that are important to gay men.

148
00:06:42.986 --> 00:06:45.226
Oh. yeah? What are you writing
about that's so important?

149
00:06:47.027 --> 00:06:48.998
I'm writing about how
gay men are being hunted

150
00:06:49.031 --> 00:06:50.635
and killed in this town.

151
00:06:50.668 --> 00:06:52.071
Wasn't us.

152
00:06:52.104 --> 00:06:54.710
All right. ladies.
it's time to go.

153
00:06:57.247 --> 00:07:00.688
-Wait. This is a... Is this a threat?
-FRAN: No.

154
00:07:00.722 --> 00:07:02.859
Sounds like you need
something to protect yourself.

155
00:07:13.146 --> 00:07:14.750
(door opens)

156
00:07:14.783 --> 00:07:16.519
Is that you?

157
00:07:18.958 --> 00:07:20.595
Something smells good.

158
00:07:20.628 --> 00:07:22.866
PATRICK: Oh. Beef Bolognese.

159
00:07:29.579 --> 00:07:30.948
How was your day?

160
00:07:30.982 --> 00:07:32.919
GINO (sighing): Oh...

161
00:07:35.858 --> 00:07:38.597
Really? I didn't know
our mayor liked boys.

162
00:07:38.631 --> 00:07:41.670
(laughs) Homophobic
Hall of Shame.

163
00:07:41.704 --> 00:07:44.008
First annual issue.

164
00:07:44.041 --> 00:07:46.814
You should thank me
for not including you.

165
00:07:46.847 --> 00:07:48.818
- Funny.
- Seriously.

166
00:07:48.851 --> 00:07:51.155
Your precinct has more
complaints from the community

167
00:07:51.189 --> 00:07:52.926
than any other
precinct in Manhattan.

168
00:07:52.959 --> 00:07:55.163
It's just a lot of old-school
guys all in one place.

169
00:07:55.197 --> 00:07:57.000
Keep defending them.

170
00:07:57.034 --> 00:07:59.773
You should quit and
do something else.

171
00:07:59.806 --> 00:08:01.844
I don't know how to
do anything else.

172
00:08:02.846 --> 00:08:04.850
That's not exactly true.

173
00:08:04.883 --> 00:08:06.920
(Patrick chuckles)

174
00:08:12.932 --> 00:08:14.803
What's the matter?
You look tense.

175
00:08:14.836 --> 00:08:17.141
We found another body.

176
00:08:18.109 --> 00:08:20.648
By the piers. He
was missing a head.

177
00:08:20.681 --> 00:08:22.952
What the fuck?

178
00:08:24.689 --> 00:08:26.560
Oh. Jesus. Patrick.

179
00:08:26.593 --> 00:08:28.764
- That's three now.
- Mm-hmm.

180
00:08:28.798 --> 00:08:30.735
Is the department gonna
hold a press conference?

181
00:08:30.768 --> 00:08:32.147
- People need to know about this.
- No.

182
00:08:32.171 --> 00:08:33.841
And I am telling you
this off the record.

183
00:08:33.874 --> 00:08:36.847
I'm not supposed to talk
about this with anyone.

184
00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:38.851
I'm not "anyone."

185
00:08:38.884 --> 00:08:40.855
I'm the guy you supposedly love.

186
00:08:40.888 --> 00:08:42.792
I should be writing about...

187
00:08:42.826 --> 00:08:45.798
Hell. the New York Times
should be writing about it.

188
00:08:45.832 --> 00:08:47.902
- and you should be helping.
- I-I can't.

189
00:08:47.936 --> 00:08:49.338
Gino. we have talked about this.

190
00:08:49.371 --> 00:08:51.018
We have to keep our
professional lives separate.

191
00:08:51.042 --> 00:08:53.079
Oh. really? When
it's life-and-death?

192
00:08:53.113 --> 00:08:55.193
- Those are the rules?
- Just think what you want to think.

193
00:08:55.217 --> 00:08:59.125
But I am not going to jeopardize
my career to be your source.

194
00:08:59.158 --> 00:09:01.797
The fuck good are you?

195
00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:03.133
(Gino sighs)

196
00:09:03.166 --> 00:09:06.038
What the fuck am I doing?

197
00:09:06.072 --> 00:09:08.878
- What am I doing?
- What are you talking about?

198
00:09:08.911 --> 00:09:12.017
What the fuck am
I doing with you?

199
00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:15.190
Here in this sham
of a relationship?

200
00:09:15.223 --> 00:09:16.660
Hey. hey. hey. no.
Don't say that.

201
00:09:16.693 --> 00:09:18.129
It's not a sham. okay?

202
00:09:18.163 --> 00:09:19.733
I did not go through everything

203
00:09:19.766 --> 00:09:21.068
that I've gone
through in my life

204
00:09:21.102 --> 00:09:23.106
to go back into the
closet for a guy

205
00:09:23.139 --> 00:09:25.878
who does not want to
be what he truly is.

206
00:09:25.912 --> 00:09:30.120
Yeah. maybe. but I
am very good in bed.

207
00:09:32.357 --> 00:09:33.794
(soft chuckle)

208
00:09:37.969 --> 00:09:40.307
(sighs)

209
00:09:43.213 --> 00:09:45.317
Gino...

210
00:09:48.122 --> 00:09:50.227
I am doing the best I can.

211
00:09:54.335 --> 00:09:55.838
Maybe that's just...

212
00:09:55.872 --> 00:09:58.644
That's not enough.

213
00:09:58.677 --> 00:10:00.648
We need you.

214
00:10:00.681 --> 00:10:02.184
I need you.

215
00:10:07.962 --> 00:10:10.000
Not like this.

216
00:10:11.068 --> 00:10:13.039
Where are you going?

217
00:10:13.072 --> 00:10:15.177
Somewhere.

218
00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:17.882
- Anywhere where I'm not hiding.
- Mm.

219
00:10:17.916 --> 00:10:20.120
Or helping someone to hide.

220
00:10:21.289 --> 00:10:24.361
Come on. Gino. Let's just...

221
00:10:24.395 --> 00:10:25.898
(door opens)

222
00:10:25.932 --> 00:10:27.669
(door closes)

223
00:10:29.071 --> 00:10:31.275
(sighs) Shit.

224
00:10:34.850 --> 00:10:36.787
SHERIFF (on TV): Mr. Ewing?

225
00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:38.958
- Yeah.
- Mr. Barnes made a very serious accusation.

226
00:10:38.991 --> 00:10:40.704
He claims you pushed Miss
Shepard off that balcony.

227
00:10:40.728 --> 00:10:42.097
J.R.: That man is a damn liar.

228
00:10:42.130 --> 00:10:43.934
I saw him...

229
00:10:43.968 --> 00:10:45.437
ADAM: I was watching that.

230
00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:47.174
Mm. Come on. Get
yourself cleaned up.

231
00:10:47.207 --> 00:10:49.111
You're coming out with me.

232
00:10:49.144 --> 00:10:51.249
I don't want to go anywhere.

233
00:10:52.284 --> 00:10:54.355
Fuck off. Sully.

234
00:10:54.388 --> 00:10:56.368
You have been eating breakfast
cereal and watching TV

235
00:10:56.392 --> 00:10:58.263
for six days.

236
00:10:58.296 --> 00:11:02.037
Adam. I could understand one day
'cause of his hot little accent.

237
00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:05.210
but any longer is just you
feeling sorry for yourself.

238
00:11:05.243 --> 00:11:07.749
I was falling in love with him.

239
00:11:07.782 --> 00:11:10.086
Bullshit. You were falling
in love with falling in love.

240
00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:12.157
Get off of me.

241
00:11:13.359 --> 00:11:15.330
I really need you tonight.

242
00:11:15.363 --> 00:11:16.867
I got to do some business.

243
00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:18.279
and I don't want to
go out there alone.

244
00:11:18.303 --> 00:11:20.407
Are those drugs?

245
00:11:20.440 --> 00:11:22.077
What's the hurry
with selling ludes?

246
00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:24.114
The price is skyrocketing.
I really need the money.

247
00:11:24.148 --> 00:11:25.985
and you really need
some fresh air.

248
00:11:26.987 --> 00:11:28.757
Fine.

249
00:11:28.791 --> 00:11:31.863
Where are we going?
What is this?

250
00:11:31.897 --> 00:11:34.134
Only one of the best
places in the world.

251
00:11:34.168 --> 00:11:36.372
(indistinct shouting)

252
00:11:36.405 --> 00:11:38.376
You're not here to sell
those pills. are you?

253
00:11:38.409 --> 00:11:40.247
Okay. so maybe I lied.

254
00:11:40.280 --> 00:11:42.451
Had to get you off
that couch. okay?

255
00:11:42.484 --> 00:11:44.421
- This is dirty.
